  "courseSlug": "react-native-the-practical-guide",
  "courseTitle": "React Native - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197310",
      "title": "What Is React Native?",
      "lectureOrder": 2,
      "videoOrder": 2,
      "sourceHash": "6f36d8e19a354eb2bd15c345c531741b5ff03a23edc67070a83bcff59859157c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.23,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "So, what exactly is React Native?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 7.33,
          "end": 12.33,
          "en": "Well, as the name applies, it is related to React.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 12.59,
          "end": 16.54,
          "en": "And with React.js and React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 16.54,
          "end": 20.81,
          "en": "you can build real React Native based mobile apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 20.81,
          "end": 22.67,
          "en": "for iOS and Android,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.67,
          "end": 26.01,
          "en": "which are real apps you can distribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 26.01,
          "end": 28.91,
          "en": "through the app stores and apps that can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.91,
          "end": 32.8,
          "en": "by any user with an iOS or Android device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.8,
          "end": 36.91,
          "en": "Now React.js is a library that's independent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 36.91,
          "end": 39.24,
          "en": "from React Native though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.24,
          "end": 42.09,
          "en": "React.js is a JavaScript library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.09,
          "end": 45.03,
          "en": "for building user interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.03,
          "end": 48.43,
          "en": "And it is typically used for web development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.43,
          "end": 52.626,
          "en": "That's also the environment for which it was first created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.626,
          "end": 56.18,
          "en": "But actually, if you worked with React.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 56.18,
          "end": 60.45,
          "en": "you might know that there, it's actually another library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.45,
          "end": 65.353,
          "en": "the React DOM library that adds the actual web support",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 65.353,
          "end": 70.353,
          "en": "because React itself, the library React itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 70.46000000000001,
          "end": 74.83,
          "en": "without React DOM is platform-agnostic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 74.83,
          "end": 77.251,
          "en": "which means you can use React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 77.251,
          "end": 81.16,
          "en": "in conjunction with React DOM to build web apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 81.16,
          "end": 85.05,
          "en": "but React the library itself, actually does not care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 85.05,
          "end": 87.3,
          "en": "about the underlying platform.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 87.3,
          "end": 90.75,
          "en": "React just gives you tools for managing state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 90.75,
          "end": 93.64,
          "en": "for building virtual component trees,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 93.64,
          "end": 97.38,
          "en": "and then you need an extra library like React DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 97.38,
          "end": 101.49600000000001,
          "en": "for translating the result React produced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 101.49600000000001,
          "end": 105.68,
          "en": "to an actual platform like the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 105.68,
          "end": 108.33,
          "en": "Now, React Native is basically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 108.33,
          "end": 112.44,
          "en": "an alternative to React DOM, therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 112.44,
          "end": 114.63,
          "en": "React Native gives you a collection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 114.63,
          "end": 117.35,
          "en": "of special react components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 117.35,
          "end": 120.18,
          "en": "which you can use in your JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 120.18,
          "end": 124.84,
          "en": "So React Native ships with built-in components you can use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 124.84,
          "end": 129.84,
          "en": "And those components are then compiled to native UI elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 130.8,
          "end": 134.17,
          "en": "for the iOS and Android platforms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 134.17,
          "end": 136.29,
          "en": "and React Native will also take care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 136.29,
          "end": 139.35,
          "en": "about this compilation step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 139.35,
          "end": 141.03,
          "en": "In addition, React Native",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 141.03,
          "end": 145.47,
          "en": "also exposes certain native platform APIs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 145.47,
          "end": 147.89,
          "en": "like using the device camera",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 147.89,
          "end": 152.186,
          "en": "so that you can use such features in your JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 152.186,
          "end": 154.22,
          "en": "even though you need to tap",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 154.22,
          "end": 157.52,
          "en": "into native device APIs for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 157.52,
          "end": 161.88,
          "en": "And therefore in the end, React Native is like React DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 161.88,
          "end": 166.64,
          "en": "It just does not target the web, the browser as a platform,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 166.64,
          "end": 169.32,
          "en": "but instead iOS and Android.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 169.32,
          "end": 170.72,
          "en": "And React Native gives you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 170.72,
          "end": 174.82,
          "en": "all the components and the APIs you need to interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 174.82,
          "end": 179.4,
          "en": "with those platforms and to build apps for those platforms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 179.4,
          "end": 182.52,
          "en": "That is what React Native is all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 182.52,
          "end": 186.43,
          "en": "And therefore, in order to work with React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 186.43,
          "end": 189.57,
          "en": "you also must know React.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 189.57,
          "end": 192.66,
          "en": "because you will write your code in React.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 192.66,
          "end": 196.67000000000002,
          "en": "and then just use these extra React Native components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 196.67000000000002,
          "end": 200.637,
          "en": "and APIs in your React JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 200.637,
          "end": 203.578,
          "en": "to produce those native mobile apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 203.578,
          "end": 205.763,
          "en": "for iOS and Android.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
